#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""mose -- check, build and launch a MOSE_GPU case from its own input.ini.

  mose check  [CASE]                  what the case needs and whether the GPU build runs it
  mose build  [CASE]                  make sure the matching binary exists (submits its build job if not)
  mose solve  [CASE] [-n N] [-p PART] [-t TIME] [-J NAME] [--mem MEM] [--nodelist NODE] [--dry-run]
  mose list                           the binaries already built
  mose example                        print an annotated GPU input.ini

CASE is the case folder (default: the current one): input.ini + INPUT/. -p is the SLURM partition the run goes to, the
GPU nodes it runs on (default fatgpu). `mose submit` is the old name of `mose solve`. A wrong or incomplete command is
answered with what was probably meant; scripts/mose_completion.sh adds Tab completion.

The binary is chosen from the case, nothing is set by hand:
  species count         lines after the first of INPUT/phase.txt (the count FLINT reads)
  turbulence equations  [MOSE-RANS] turbulence-model (no RANS section = Euler), or in the MOSE_open dialect
                        [MOSE-Physics] equations + turbulence
  chemistry integrator  [MOSE-ODE] solver = H-radau5 (default) or H-rodas ([MOSE-Chemistry] ode-solver)
A case written in the MOSE_open dialect ([MOSE-Parameters], [MOSE-Numerics], [MOSE-Physics] equations) runs as it is:
the code translates it at start-up (src/lib/io/IO_Ini_Open.f90) and stops with a message on what the GPU lacks;
`mose check` applies the same rules before the queue.
Each combination is built once per state of the source tree with the certified recipe
`install.sh build --production --nsc=N --nrans=R [--ode-rodas]` (a job on the free partition, ~3 min),
kept read-only in $MOSE_BUILDS (default /scratch/$USER/mose_builds) and reused by every later run.
The run job waits for the build job (--dependency=afterok) when the binary is not there yet.

Environment: MOSE_SRC (source tree to build, default: the tree this script is in), MOSE_BUILDS,
MOSE_BUILD_PARTITION (default free). Python 3.6+, standard library only.
"""
